{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A cycle basis: the fundamental cycles of the breadth-first spanning forest, one for each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge outside the forest, in ascending position of that edge, so "},{"code":"edgeCount - vertexCount + c","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cycles for c components. Roots are taken in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order and edges in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order; a vertex’s tree edge is the one that discovered it. Self-loops and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parallel edges are supported: a loop is a cycle of its own, and a second copy of an edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closes a cycle of length 2."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/cycleBasis()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"title":"cycleBasis()","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Cycles"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cycleBasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Cycle"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":">]"}],"symbolKind":"method","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/